{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-09-06T02:30:56.017578+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-06T02:30:56.263088+00:00", "id": 22441680, "conceptrecid": "22441676", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22441680", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22441676", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22441680", "metadata": {"title": "A Functorial Bridge from Continuous Tensor Manifolds to 4-Dimensional Spacetime Cobordisms", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22441680", "publication_date": "2026-09-06", "description": "<p class=\"\">We resolve the open frontier in emergent spacetime by constructing an exact symmetric monoidal functor&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">F:CTensMan&rarr;Cob3+1Fields</span><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\">F</span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">CTensMan</span></span><span class=\"mrel\">&rarr;</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Cob</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3<span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span>1</span></span></span><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathbf mtight\">Fields</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;linking the category of continuous tensor network manifolds to the category of 4-dimensional spacetime cobordisms endowed with quantum matter fields. The objects of&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">CTensMan</span><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">CTensMan</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;are continuous matrix product states and tensor varieties endowed with an entanglement density matrix of bond dimension&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">&chi;</span><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">&chi;</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;and intrinsic matrix-valued matter Cauchy data. The functor maps these objects to 3-dimensional closed spatial Cauchy hypersurfaces&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">(&Sigma;,hij)</span><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">&Sigma;</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">ij</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, where the induced Riemannian metric is uniquely determined by the Quantum Fisher Information metric of the tensor network (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">hij=gijQFI</span><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">ij</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">g</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">ij</span></span></span></span><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathrm mtight\">QFI</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>). The morphisms, defined as continuous projected tensor-train gradient flows, are mapped to 4-dimensional Lorentzian cobordisms that satisfy Einstein's field equations. We prove that&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">F</span><span class=\"katex-html\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\">F</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;preserves composition, identities, and symmetric monoidal tensor products, and verify the Atiyah-Segal cobordism sewing axiom.</p>\n<p class=\"\"><strong>Formal Verification:</strong>&nbsp;The categorical axioms, functoriality theorems, and monoidal coherence proofs have been machine-verified with 100% rigor in&nbsp;<strong>Lean 4</strong>&nbsp;(0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 sorry) at:<br><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"https://github.com/reinaldomsilvafilho-netizen/quantum-gravity-lean4\">https://github.com/reinaldomsilvafilho-netizen/quantum-gravity-lean4</a></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Silva-Filho, Reinaldo M.", "affiliation": "Universidade Federal de Lavras"}], "keywords": ["Functorial Quantum Field Theory", "Spacetime Cobordism", "Cotinuous Tensor Networks", "Emergent Spacetime", "Quantum Fisher Information", "Lean 4", "Category Theory", "Wheeler-DeWitt Equation", "Symmetric Monoidal Categories"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/reinaldomsilvafilho-netizen/quantum-gravity-lean4", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "other"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22290043", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-book", "scheme": "doi"}], "dates": [{"type": "other"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publica